 "frozen_rule": "Frozen before replay (2026-10-26T01:53Z). No new code, no thresholds: existing opt-ins.\nBinary: develop 2e224ea. Recipes: default, CDM (= CD + --max-position-jump-motion-compensation),\nCDMH (= CDM + --hold-kalman-update).\nMechanism (PPC tokyo/run2): CDM stays in a hold-fix streak 0.28-0.44 m off for ~24 s from TOW 177058.8\n(legacy hold overwrite keeps the biased basin) and then loses 55 default-correct epochs (lambda_not_fixed).\nPrediction: under CDMH that streak is shorter and the default-correct loss on tokyo/run2 is < 2%.\nGate for CDMH vs default (docs/fix_recovery_guard.md, every run, including the decrease clause): wrong FIX\n>0.5/2/3 m not increased; default-correct loss <= 1% (0.5 m); missing and horizontal P95 not increased;\nrecovery P95 and right-censoring not increased; at least one wrong-FIX population decreases.\nRuns: PPC tokyo/nagoya run1-3 (development), Trimble Odaiba/Shinjuku (development), u-blox Odaiba/Shinjuku\n(holdout), HK Deep/Harsh (descriptive, 2/3 m). Reference only for scoring. No retuning after the replay.\n",
